# Backend private methods

When adding or changing C# in `api/` or `worker/`, put every private method
in one `#region Private Methods` at the end of its type. Do this in the same
change as the method.

- The region holds private methods only. Fields, constants, and constructors
  stay above it.
- Public and internal methods stay above the region.
- One region per type. Skip the region when the type has no private methods.
- Do not nest a data type in the class. See
  `.cursor/rules/backend-type-files.mdc`.
- Do not add regions to generated EF Core migration files.

```csharp
public async Task<AccountDto> GetAccountAsync(...)
{
    return await ProjectAccountAsync(...);
}

#region Private Methods

/// <summary>
/// Loads the API shape of one household account.
/// </summary>
private async Task<AccountDto> ProjectAccountAsync(...)
{
}

#endregion
```
